rsdsk on OS-9 -- what was changed================================Bob Devries' rsdsk, 1997, "may be freely distributed".  ORIG/ holds therelease as it came out of the LHa archive, unpacked by this disk's own`lha'.NOTHING WAS CHANGED.  Like its sibling os9dsk it was written for OS-9 andships a makefile.68000; this is a rebuild from that source.  The recipefollows the makefile: ten sources, no extra library.WHAT IT READS.  The RS-DOS side of a CoCo .DSK image -- Disk Extended BASICdisks, where a name is eight characters and three, and a file is BASIC, abinary, data or text.  The sample image in DOC/rsdsk lists MENU.BAS,ORCH.BIN, ORCH.DOC and a handful of music files.There is no option to write: it reads a disk image and copies files out ofit, and that is all it claims to do.